@item00 @wire_accountability @spec:1722-7.3.3
Feature: Advertised channels_per_frame is a width the fabric can emit # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:42

  @item00 @wire_accountability @spec:1722-7.3.3
  Feature: Advertised channels_per_frame is a width the fabric can emit  # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:42

  Scenario: the shipping stereo config is self-consistent (negative control)   # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:47
    Given the end-station builder is importable                                # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_arty_current"                     # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    Then every AAF talker format's channels_per_frame equals the emitted width # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:91

  Scenario: the 8x8 config advertises 8 channels and the fabric emits 8       # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:54
    Given the end-station builder is importable                               # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_ax7101_8x8"                      # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    Then the declared talker width is 8 channels                              # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:83
    And every AAF talker format's channels_per_frame equals the emitted width # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:91

  Scenario: the 4x4 config advertises 4 channels and the fabric emits 4       # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:59
    Given the end-station builder is importable                               # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_arty_4x4"                        # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    Then the declared talker width is 4 channels                              # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:83
    And every AAF talker format's channels_per_frame equals the emitted width # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:91

  Scenario Outline: the generated wire constant matches the derivation -- @1.1   # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:73
    Given the end-station builder is importable                                  # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_arty_current"                       # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    Then the generated TALKER_WIRE_CHANS_C equals the emitted width              # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:120

  Scenario Outline: the generated wire constant matches the derivation -- @1.2   # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:74
    Given the end-station builder is importable                                  # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_arty_4x4"                           # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    Then the generated TALKER_WIRE_CHANS_C equals the emitted width              # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:120

  Scenario Outline: the generated wire constant matches the derivation -- @1.3   # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:75
    Given the end-station builder is importable                                  # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_ax7101_8x8"                         # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
