  Scenario: an unbacked audio interface does not silently change the gateware  # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:77
    Given the end-station builder is importable                                # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_ax7101_8x8"                       # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    When the TDM bus is not backed by the fabric                               # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:67
    Then the audio interface is reported as a placeholder                      # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:137
    And the emitted width falls back to 2 channels                             # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:150

  Scenario: with the TDM master present the interface is backed  # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:88
    Given the end-station builder is importable                  # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
    Given the end-station config "endstation_ax7101_8x8"         # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:58
    When the TDM bus is backed by the fabric                     # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:73
    Then the audio interface is not a placeholder                # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:143
    And the soc argv carries "--audio-interface"                 # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:165
    And the soc argv carries "--audio-interface-master"          # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:165

  Scenario: the derivation REFUSES to over-declare (negative control)  # features/wire_channel_accountability.feature:97
    Given the end-station builder is importable                        # steps/wire_accountability_steps.py:45
